findings.body:
`FormWrapper` now reads `openForm.in_reply_to_snippet` without optional chaining. `MainForm` renders `<FormWrapper>` without an `openForm` prop, so `openForm` is `undefined`. `MainForm` sets `isOpen = editor?.isFocused || hasContent`, so focusing the top-level comment box evaluates `openForm.in_reply_to_snippet` and throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`. The change to `openForm?.` was unnecessary for the bug fix and should be reverted.

::diff{file="apps/comments-ui/src/components/content/forms/form.tsx" lines="311-315"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The main form (`main-form.tsx:79`) passes no `openForm`. This affects every visitor who clicks into the main comment box, so it is a blocking regression.

::suggestion{file="apps/comments-ui/src/components/content/forms/form.tsx" lines="313-313"}
const isReplyToReply = !!openForm?.in_reply_to_snippet;

Replacing `openForm.in_reply_to_id` with `parent.id` changes the reply target. For a reply-to-reply, `comment.tsx` sets `openForm.in_reply_to_id` to the reply being answered, but the form is rendered inside the top-level `PublishedComment`, so `parent` is the top-level comment. The new code posts the reply with `in_reply_to_id` equal to the top-level comment's id, which drops the 'replying to' link and misattributes the reply in threads with multiple nested replies. The `openForm` dependency was also removed from `useCallback`, which hides the stale value.

::diff{file="apps/comments-ui/src/components/content/forms/reply-form.tsx" lines="27-36"}

The header fix does not need this change. The `in_reply_to_id` edit should be reverted and `openForm` restored in the dependency array.

The editor-enable gate changed from `!!memberName` to `!!member?.expertise`. The comment above the line still says 'Disable editing if the member doesn't have a name'. This is not described in the PR and it changes the behavior for members who have a name but no expertise. Those users now get a non-editable reply editor, even though `focusEditor` only forces the name prompt when the name is missing. The first new e2e test (`expertise: null`) then depends on the editor getting focus while it is non-editable, so it is worth checking whether it passes for the right reason.

::diff{file="apps/comments-ui/src/components/content/forms/form.tsx" lines="262-265"}

If expertise gating is intended, update the comment and the PR description and state why. If not, revert to `memberName`.
